subproblem.statement:
Let m be a natural number and R^m := Rn m = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin m). Write B°_r(x) for the open ball (Metric.ball). Let D be a subset of R^m, c a point of R^m and R a real number with R > 0. Assume:
(a) D is closed;
(b) c ∈ D;
(c) for every w ∈ D ∩ B°_R(c) there is ε > 0 with B°_ε(w) ∩ B°_R(c) ⊆ D.
Then B°_R(c) ⊆ D.
